o  just forget about everything they just  think of the nature we can say they can  hear the silence the tents were designed  in the United States a steel geodesic  dome provides stability against the wind  and snow  a wood stove provides heat retained  inside by triple insulation the staff  keep the stoves burning during the day  but at night the job is up to the guests  you can heat the pot inside up to 25  degrees easily the thing is that you  still have to wake up during the night  otherwise it's going to be pretty cool  in the morning but that's part of the  experience of white buds and actually  people like it after sunset the guests  can retire to their tents or dine in the  resort's own restaurant nearby  after a long exhausting hike through the  snowy winter woods Selina Balin bold and  chilly bajji enjoy a traditional Swiss  fondue the perfect end to a perfect day  now they're hoping for a clear night  with a view of the Milky Way from their  cozy abode
 

